Why Is Demand Increasing
AI and HPC workloads: Data centers require greater memory bandwidth and capacity for AI, ML and big-data workloads.
Hyperscale expansion: Expansion of hyperscale facilities is increasing demand for high-density memory modules.
DDR5 transition: Higher-speed and more energy-efficient DDR5 DRAM is accelerating market adoption.
Fab & Technology Pulse

The DRAM technology race is increasingly centered on capacity, bandwidth, latency and power efficiency. RDIMM and LRDIMM modules are important for high-performance server environments because they provide higher capacity and lower latency. High-capacity LRDIMMs capable of exceeding 256GB per module are being developed for hyperscale applications. Meanwhile, DDR5 technology is improving speed and energy efficiency as data-center operators scale AI and cloud infrastructure.

